      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Bone metastases require multidisciplinary treatment, the primary goal of which is to relieve pain and improve quality of life. Among the options available, bone-seeking radioisotopes are attractive because they can treat several symptomatic metastases simultaneously. This therapy may have antitumor efficacy in addition to analgesic properties. Although the ultimate place of systemic radionuclides in the treatment of bone metastases has not been firmly established, some patients clearly benefit from these modalities."},
